{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "e2gnPma9Epi8-PgFa",
			"description": "Psychic Hood",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A warded circlet built around a tiny, heavily sanctioned psychic node (sometimes a bound, lobotomised psyker's brain-stem), worn by Astra Militarum officers and Inquisitorial staff to blunt enemy sorcery directed at their command. Consistent with Dark Heresy/Rogue Trader's psychic hood/psy-focus items and Codex background on Imperial command-squad wargear.\n\nDesign: Modelled as a flat +2 conditional bonus (Basic's conditional_modifier feature) to resist Warp Sorcery-tagged mental attacks — comparable in size to Basic's own Power Defense-type items, cheap enough to matter but never a substitute for a trained anti-psyker.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "4000",
			"base_weight": "3 lb",
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "conditional_modifier",
					"situation": "to resist Warp Sorcery-tagged Affliction, Mind Control, Mind Probe, and Fear effects directed at the wearer or their unit",
					"amount": 2
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eLLWNnk4MyzhdOmLh",
			"description": "Force Sword",
			"local_notes": "Human-scale pattern, for Inquisitors and other unaugmented psykers. Astartes Librarians use the Astartes pattern below.\n\nLore: A disruption-field blade further warded and psychically attuned so a trained mind can channel force directly through it — standard wargear for Inquisitors and for Sisters of the Ordo Hereticus with psychic gifts. Depicted throughout Black Library (Eisenhorn's own force sword; Grey Knights' force weapons) and Dark Heresy/Rogue Trader's force-weapon rules.\n\nDesign: Built directly on the framework's power-field rule: field off is the mundane fine blade (sw+1 cut), field on adds +3d and armour divisor (10) (\"Bladed/mace power weapons add +3d over the mundane weapon\"), landing exactly on the Power Sword anchor (sw+3d+1(10) cut) — a force sword is mechanically a power sword that a trained mind can also channel psychic force through. The Force Strike line shows that channelling: same dice as field-on minus the armour divisor, but its ignores-DR component only applies against Warp-touched targets, so it never trivialises ordinary armour. Its damage scales with the wielder's Psyker Talent level (+1d per level on top of the base 3d) rather than as a fixed number, since the build tool's damage syntax cannot encode a variable. Handling: 4 lb, min ST 10 and parry 0 match the human Power Sword anchor exactly (Broadsword, a guarded blade rather than an axe/mace weapon).",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "8000",
			"base_weight": "4 lb",
