			"id": "eIUNZAJPG2HTP8g3L",
			"description": "Nemesis Force Halberd",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The signature weapon of the Grey Knights: a psychically-attuned halberd that is, to a daemon, as lethal as a bolt round is to a man — Codex: Grey Knights and its Black Library tie-ins (Ben Counter's Grey Knights novels) are consistent on this. Nemesis weapons are built and sanctified specifically to hurt things from the warp.\n\nDesign: Same mundane baseline and power-field math (+3d, armour divisor (10)) as the Force Axe, reach 1-2 like other polearms, priced and LC0'd as unique Chapter-restricted wargear per the framework's LC table (Astartes/Inquisition-only warp-touched gear). Its Force Strike line waives the normal Perils check as a narrative nod to how routinely and safely Grey Knights use it against their signature enemy, unlike a general-purpose force weapon. Handling: Grey Knights are Astartes, so the halberd is built at Astartes scale: 14 lb and min ST 14, level with the Astartes Chainsword (14 lb/ST 15) and close to the Power Axe (13 lb/ST 18) in melee.yaml, reflecting a two-handed haft weapon rather than a single-handed blade or axe-head. Parry 0U, the Basic Set convention for a polearm: halberd-class weapons are unbalanced and slow to recover, as axes and mauls are.",
